#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:16
msgid "Manipulating animation frames"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:17
msgid "LET'S GET STARTED!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:19
msgid "In this tour, you'll learn how to manipulate individual frames in the SpriteFrames editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:22
msgid "You'll create an animation of a character blinking occasionally."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:40
msgid "Creating a new animation"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:46
msgid "It's common in games to have an idle animation with the character mostly standing still and blinking occasionally. That's what we'll create in this tour."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:47
msgid "Click the %s [b]New Animation[/b] button at the top left of the editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:50
msgid "Add Animation"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:53
msgid "Renaming the new animation"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:59
msgid "Animations are created with the default name [b]new_animation[/b]. This could be clearer so let's rename it."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:60
msgid "Click on [b]new_animation[/b] in the animation list to rename it. Type [b]idle[/b] and press Enter."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:64
msgid "Rename [b]new_animation[/b] to [b]idle[/b]"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:78
msgid "The idle animation frames"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:84
msgid "For the idle animation, we'll use two frames to make the character blink occasionally: one where the character is standing with open eyes and one where her eyes are closed."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:85
msgid "In the [b]FileSystem[/b] dock, find and select the idle animation images ([b]idle.png[/b] and [b]blinking.png[/b]). You can press the [b]Crtl[/b] key ([b]Cmd[/b] on macOS) before clicking to add a file to the selection."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:89
msgid "Select the [b]blinking.png[/b] and [b]idle.png[/b] files in the [b]FileSystem[/b] dock"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:109
msgid "Adding the idle frames"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:116
msgid "Drag and drop the selected idle images into the [b]Frames View[/b] of the SpriteFrames editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:117
msgid "You should end with two frames in the [b]Frames View[/b]: one for the standing pose and one for the blinking pose."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:121
msgid "Add the standing and blinking frames to the animation."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:142
msgid "Reordering the frames"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:148
msgid "The frames were added based on their order in the [b]FileSystem[/b] dock: the blinking frame first, and the standing frame second."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:149
msgid "For our idle animation, we need to swap them: the standing pose should be frame [b]0[/b] (the first frame), and the blinking pose frame [b]1[/b] (the second frame)."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:150
msgid "You can reorder the frames by dragging and dropping them within the [b]Frames View[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:154
msgid "Ensure the standing pose is frame [b]0[/b] and the blinking pose is frame [b]1[/b]"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:167
msgid "Previewing the animation"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:173
msgid "Good job! Now, click the %s [b]Play[/b] icon to preview the animation."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:174
msgid "As both frames have the same duration, the result looks off: the character blinks continuously."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:175
msgid "Instead, we want the character to only blink occasionally, so we need to adjust the timing of these frames."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:178
#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:220
msgid "Play the animation."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:181
msgid "Adjusting individual frame duration"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:190
msgid "We can adjust the duration of individual frames using the [b]Frame Duration[/b] field in the toolbar above the frames view."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:191
msgid "In the [b]Frames View[/b], select the frame [b]0[/b] (the standing pose)."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:192
msgid "With the frame selected, head to the [b]Frame Duration[/b] field at the top right of the SpriteFrames editor."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:193
msgid "Change the value from [b]1.0[/b] to [b]20.0[/b] and press [b]Enter[/b]. This makes this frame stay on screen 20 times longer than the default duration."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:197
msgid "Change the [b]Frame Duration[/b] of the frame [b]0[/b] to [b]20.0[/b]"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:210
msgid "Previewing the adjusted animation"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:216
msgid "Click the %s [b]Play[/b] button again to preview the animation with the adjusted timing."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:217
msgid "Now the character stays in the standing pose for much longer and only blinks occasionally. This is more natural!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:223
msgid "Creating a blinking pattern"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:229
msgid "Now let's make the character blink twice in a row before returning to the long idle pose. It'll make the animation nicer and it'll teach you how to copy and paste frames."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:230
msgid "First, we have to select the frames we want to copy."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:231
msgid "Click on the first frame, then hold [b]Shift[/b] and click on the second frame to select both frames."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:235
msgid "Select both animation frames"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:242
#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:257
msgid "Pasting frames"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:251
msgid "With both frames selected, click the %s [b]Copy Frames[/b] button above the [b]Frames View[/b] to copy the frames in the clipboard."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:266
msgid "Now click the %s [b]Paste Frames[/b] button. This duplicates the copied frames and inserts them at the end of the animation."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:272
msgid "The updated animation"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:278
msgid "Click the %s [b]Play[/b] button to preview the animation."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:279
msgid "Copying and pasting the frames duplicated our animation. The character waits for a long time, blinks, and repeats the pattern."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:280
msgid "We can adjust the third frame's duration to make the character blink twice in a row."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:285
msgid "Changing the second idle pose duration"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:294
msgid "Click on frame [b]2[/b] (the second standing pose) to select it. Then, change the [b]Frame Duration[/b] from [b]20.0[/b] to [b]2.0[/b]."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:295
msgid "This will result in a much shorter idle pose and make the character blink twice in a row before returning to the long idle pose."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:299
msgid "Change the [b]Frame Duration[/b] of frame [b]2[/b] to [b]2.0[/b]"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:308
msgid "Previewing the idle animation"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:314
msgid "Click the [b]Play[/b] button to preview the idle animation with the adjusted timing."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:315
msgid "It looks much nicer, doesn't it?"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:318
msgid "Play"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:321
msgid "Reviewing what we've done"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:326
msgid "Let's review how we created the idle animation:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:328
msgid "Frame [b]0[/b] (the standing pose) lasts 20 frames"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:329
msgid "Frame [b]1[/b] (the first blink) shows briefly for one frame"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:330
msgid "Frame [b]2[/b] (standing pose again) lasts 2 frames"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:331
msgid "Frame [b]3[/b] (blinking again) shows briefly for one frame before the cycle repeats"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:333
msgid "All it took was 2 textures! By reordering the frames and adjusting their durations, you could create a nice idle animation."
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:340
msgid "Congratulations!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:341
msgid "CONTINUE"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:343
msgid "You've successfully learned how to use the [b]AnimatedSprite2D[/b] node and [b]SpriteFrames[/b] editor to create frame-by-frame animations!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:346
msgid "In this tour, you've learned how to:"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:348
msgid "Modify individual frame durations"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:349
msgid "Drag and drop frames in the [b]Frames View[/b] to reorder them"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:350
msgid "Copy and paste frames to duplicate them"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:354
msgid "Between the previous tour and this one, you learned the features you'll use most often in the [b]SpriteFrames[/b] editor!"
msgstr ""

#: tours/103_manipulating_frames/103_manipulating_frames.gd:355
msgid "After completing this tour, you can keep experimenting and return to GDSchool to continue with this module's lessons whenever you want."
msgstr ""
